# Custom Hooks

## Do

- Prefix every custom hook with **`use`** (e.g. `useUsers`, `useLogin`).
- Keep hooks under **`src/hooks/**`**; colocate query wrappers under **`src/hooks/query/**`**.
- One responsibility per hook; return an **object with named fields** (unless intentionally mirroring `useState`).
- Delegate HTTP to the **service layer** + shared **`apiClient`** — hooks orchestrate TanStack Query, not raw axios per endpoint in scattered places.

## Don't

- Do not call hooks **conditionally** or inside loops — follow Rules of Hooks.
- Do not **duplicate** the same `useQuery` / `useMutation` options in many files — wrap in a dedicated hook.
- Do not return auth secrets from hooks to unrelated UI.

## Security focus

- Follow global security baseline in **`000-core.mdc`**.
- Hooks that touch auth must fail gracefully when unauthenticated and must not leak credentials through return values or thrown errors.
